From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge-connector: Ask for a mode set when HDR metadata changes

A bridge outside the HDMI connector framework, such as dw-hdmi, writes
its HDR metadata InfoFrame only on a mode set. Its own connector forces
one when HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA changes; a bridge connector does not, so a
player setting the metadata at the same mode leaves the sink on the last
mode set's values: HDR over a menu, or SDR over a film.

Forcing it from a bridge's atomic_check comes too late: that runs in
mode_fixup(), after the helpers added a mode-setting CRTC's planes and
connectors to the commit. Force it here, as dw_hdmi_connector_atomic_check()
does.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_bridge_connector.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 
+#include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_state_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_bridge.h>
 #include <drm/drm_bridge_connector.h>
@@ -375,10 +376,29 @@
 {
 	struct drm_bridge_connector *bridge_connector =
 		to_drm_bridge_connector(connector);
+	struct drm_connector_state *old_state =
+		drm_atomic_get_old_connector_state(state, connector);
+	struct drm_connector_state *new_state =
+		drm_atomic_get_new_connector_state(state, connector);
+	struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state;
 
 	if (bridge_connector->bridge_hdmi)
 		return drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_check(connector, state);
 
+	/*
+	 * A bridge outside the HDMI connector framework sends its HDR metadata
+	 * InfoFrame only on a mode set: ask for one when the metadata changes,
+	 * before the helpers add the CRTC's planes and connectors to it.
+	 */
+	if (new_state->crtc &&
+	    !drm_connector_atomic_hdr_metadata_equal(old_state, new_state)) {
+		crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state, new_state->crtc);
+		if (IS_ERR(crtc_state))
+			return PTR_ERR(crtc_state);
+
+		crtc_state->mode_changed = true;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
